Subject: [android/build] dark window background, and no branding drawable

Applied to `android/build/` by `tools/setup_android.sh` AFTER it unzips
`android_source.zip`, with `patch -p1 --forward`. The unzip is `-o`, so it
overwrites every file the template carries — and this is the only committed file
under `android/build/` that differs from the pristine 4.7.2 template (measured
2026-08-20: 34 tracked files also present in the zip, 33 byte-identical, this one
different). Before this patch existed, running `setup_android.sh` on a working
clone silently reverted both hunks below and the next debug build came up with a
white flash.

Two changes, both doc 13 §2:

1. `android:windowBackground` `#050a13` on `GodotAppMainTheme`. Doc 13 §2 wants
   the app dark from the first frame: the export preset's
   `screen/background_color`, `project.godot`'s `boot_splash/bg_color` and the
   3D clear colour are all this same near-black blue, and the WINDOW background
   is the fourth surface in that chain — the one the compositor paints between
   the launcher tap and Godot's first frame. Left at the platform default it is
   `Theme.DeviceDefault`'s, which is white on a light-themed device.

2. `android:windowSplashScreenBrandingImage` removed. It points at
   `@drawable/splash_branding_image`, which nothing in this project ships and
   which the 4.7.2 template does not carry either (`res/drawable/` holds only
   what the exporter generates). It is a dangling resource reference in the
   template's own default theme.

If a Godot upgrade moves these lines, this patch FAILS TO APPLY and
`setup_android.sh` stops with the file named — which is the point of shipping
it as a patch rather than as a copy of the whole file. Re-cut it against the new
template, do not paper over it.

--- a/res/values/themes.xml
+++ b/res/values/themes.xml
@@ -5,13 +5,13 @@
 	<style name="GodotAppMainTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.NoActionBar">
 		<item name="android:windowSwipeToDismiss">false</item>
 		<item name="android:windowIsTranslucent">false</item>
+		<item name="android:windowBackground">#050a13</item>
 	</style>

 	<!-- GodotAppSplashTheme is auto-generated during export. Manual changes will be overwritten.
 		 To add custom attributes, use the "gradle_build/custom_theme_attributes" Android export option. -->
 	<style name="GodotAppSplashTheme" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
 		<item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@mipmap/icon_background</item>
-		<item name="android:windowSplashScreenBrandingImage">@drawable/splash_branding_image</item>
 		<item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon</item>
 		<item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/GodotAppMainTheme</item>
 		<item name="android:windowIsTranslucent">false</item>
